Origin: EmberBSD (AI-assisted), not submitted upstream.
Wait for POSIX thread termination, including thread-local destructors. Keep
joinable handles owned by the creator and serialize reaping with runningMutex.
Publish creation under that mutex; the worker no longer resets these handles.
Preserve the Windows lifecycle. Raw getters require external synchronization.

